  "facts": [
    "Sabuncubeli Tunnel, stretching 4,070 meters, was extended from an original 2,800-meter plan after a 2013 landslide, illustrating the engineering challenges of tunneling beneath Mount Sipylus.",
    "Opened on 11 June 2018, the tunnel cut travel time between Manisa and İzmir from 45 minutes to just 15, dramatically easing winter congestion.",
    "Built on a fault zone, the tunnel’s construction required special structural measures, a concern highlighted by Professor Hasan Sözbilir in 2012."
